Cap magic-school resist chance at 80%, forbid full (100%) immunity.
Touches: src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp, Unit::CalcAbsorbResist()

Why: WotLK's discrete-resist-bucket formula (11 buckets, 0%-100% in 10%
steps, weighted around GetEffectiveResistChance()) lets very high victim
resistance push real weight onto the 100% bucket, letting a caster be
fully, completely resisted/immune on a given cast. Player report: enemies
were sometimes shrugging off spell damage entirely. Clamp the selected
bucket index to 8 (80%) so the roll can never land on 90%/100%.

--- a/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp
@@ Unit::CalcAbsorbResist(DamageInfo& dmgInfo, bool Splited)
         while (r >= probabilitySum && i < 10)
             probabilitySum += discreteResistProbability[++i];

+        // Bonesaw: cap magic resistance at 80% and forbid full (100%) immunity.
+        if (i > 8)
+            i = 8;
+
         float damageResisted = float(damage * i / 10);
